<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    USB host intent-filter: lets Android offer "always open this app for this
    device" when a board is attached. Without a matching entry the operator has
    to grant USB permission by hand after every replug — and on a pinned kiosk
    screen that also means unpinning first, which is not something to ask of a
    technician on site.

    Vendor is always QinHeng (0x1A86 = 6790); only the product differs across
    the bridges we ship on. The list started as CH340G alone, mirroring the
    factory app's UsbUtil.findUSB, and the micromarket relay board — a CH340K —
    silently fell outside it.

      0x7523 = 29987  CH340G / CH340C   M109E control board
      0x7522 = 29986  CH340K / CH340N   micromarket relay board
      0x5523 = 21795  CH341             seen on some clone adapters
      0x55D4 = 21972  CH9102            newer bridges, kept ahead of need

    An entry that matches nothing costs nothing, so err on the side of listing
    the variant. If a board still asks for permission on every replug, read the
    vid/pid the board log prints on refresh and add the pair here.
-->
<resources>
    <usb-device vendor-id="6790" product-id="29987" />
    <usb-device vendor-id="6790" product-id="29986" />
    <usb-device vendor-id="6790" product-id="21795" />
    <usb-device vendor-id="6790" product-id="21972" />
</resources>
